Description: zink: do not use VK_EXT_color_write_enable on pvr
 zink lists VK_DYNAMIC_STATE_COLOR_WRITE_ENABLE_EXT in every graphics
 pipeline. pvr turns a dynamic color write enable into a shader-side
 lowering: meta_present.color_write_enable sets uses.fbfetch and every
 colour store reads the destination pixel back and selects per channel.
 zink only needs the state to switch all colour writes off while the
 fragment shader is disabled (rasterizer discard with a primitives
 generated query); without the extension it binds a null fragment shader
 instead, the same path as on drivers without EDS1.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
Author: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Generated-by: LLM
Forwarded: not-needed

